{title: 588 - Lord of All Nations}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #588 • MELROSE • 8.9.8.7}
{lyricist: Olive Wise Spannaus}
{composer: Frederick C. Maker}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 588}
{meta: tune MELROSE}
{meta: meter 8.9.8.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Lord [Em]of [G]all [C]nations, [G7/F]grant [Am]me [C]grace
[C]To love all [G7/F]people, [G/D]every race,
[C]And in each [F]person [Dm]may I [D7/F#]see
[C/E]My [Em]kindred [F]loved, [C]redeemed [Em/G]by [G7]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Break [Em]down [G]the [C]wall that [G7/F]would [Am]divide
[C]Thy children, [G7/F]Lord, [C/E]on [G/D]every side.
[C]My neighbor's [F]good [Dm]let me [D7/F#]pursue;
[C/E]Let [Em]Christian [C]love [Am]bind [Em/G]warm [G7]and [C]true.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Forgive [G]me, [C]Lord, where [G7/F]I [Am]have [C]erred
[C]By loveless act [G/D]and [C]thoughtless [G]word.
[C]Make me to [F]see [Em]the [Dm]wrong I [D7/F#]do
[C/E]Will [Em]crucify [Am]my [Em/G]Lord [G7]anew.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Give [Em]me [G]Thy [C]courage, [G7/F]Lord, [Am]to [C]speak
[C]Whenever strong [G/D]oppress [Am]the [G]weak.
[C]Should I myself [Em]the [Dm]victim [D7/F#]be,
[C/E]Help me [Em]forgive, [C]remembering Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]With [Em]Thine [G]own [C]love may [G7/F]I [Am]be [C]filled
[C]And by [G7/F]Thy [C/E]Holy Spirit [G]willed,
[C]That all I [F]touch, [Em]where'er [Dm]I [D7/F#]be,
[C/E]May be [Em]divinely touched [G7]by [C]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
